<article class="env-lemma" id="0BW3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BW3">Lemma <span data-tag="0BW3">49.8.3</span>.</a> If the Dedekind different of $A \to B$ is defined and $A \to B$ is flat, then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the canonical isomorphism $\mathcal{L}_{B/A} \to \omega _{B/A}$ sends $1 \in \mathcal{L}_{B/A}$ to the trace element $\tau _{B/A} \in \omega _{B/A}$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the Dedekind different is $\mathfrak {D}_{B/A} = \{ b \in B \mid b\omega _{B/A} \subset B\tau _{B/A}\} $. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first assertion follows from the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0BW1" data-tag="0BW1">49.8.1</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/0BT8" data-tag="0BT8">49.4.3</a>. The second assertion is immediate from the first and the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>